 >>[2026-10-30 18:10] align — the public difference. factshift.com is the prototype. factshift.center examines which concepts a particular set of physics can represent. The page is about/domains/factshift.center/. The creator understands the hesitance to AI and, as an engineer, can't really mind it. Center extends the prototype by agentic development, adding depth to cohesion and performance. Next on the canvas: carry the dated reader (site mount 850077ab; app submodule fffab72) and draw its outline. line-anatomy stays until that projection says the line back.
 >>[2026-10-30 19:50] prime — interaction depth in the plan. A behavior primes or actualizes. The nub's three levels are the tool menu, a tool's cards, and a card's controls. Primed is what → would take (tool-primed.ts); actualized writes the line or a change the line or the address can say. Pressure is not read from the device; distance, speed, hold, and pinch are the magnitudes already in hand. Annotation is one sentence per act, and that sentence is the accessible name. A stepped level is still only a ring. Open: the accessibility-tree check, the keyboard walk, and whether a drawn tie may later pull.
 >>[2026-10-30 20:10] align — the interaction note moved to INTERACTION.md after a check against the app. A tile tap opens; a hold names the swipe →, and the swipe takes it. Among a card's controls, ↑ ↓ carry into the next card. Pulling ties from this layout are accesses, follows, charges, bond, resonance, and a drawn link; holds is not emitted. Pocket layout is 40rem, and the mode squares match the title box. A coarse pointer only hides keyboard hints. A trackpad pinch on the canvas resizes nodes; it zooms over the lens. The zero-strength ties are not called priming. That reading is not the creator's.
